The baseline is clean: `npm --prefix .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer run check` returned exit 0 with 98 passing tests. A read-only reproduction confirmed the defect: input-only usage became `{cacheRead: 0, cacheWrite: 0, totalInput: 500}` and incremented requests and costs without any unmeasured counter. I’m adding the regression assertions first so they provide a real red control before the implementation edit.
